This would allow for dynamic same-turn tool updates to all **_AVAILABLE_** tools vs only allowing updates of _currently loaded_ tools

---

I realize that this is something that can _technically_ be done similarly with `activeTools`... The benefit this approach provides is allowing dynamic updates of `tools` to enable otherwise not loaded tools during runtime of the same model turn, which is probably an edge case that only applies if you have an architecture that uses a tool registry and want to allow for more dynamic selection of tools. I would argue this is likely superior approach if you are making use of subagents. 

**_Or put more simply_**: this allows for more fine grained control of what tools a theoretical `toolSearch` tool can select from. _In theory_, this would even allow for dynamically creating and using tools in a single turn

