@heiwen Great point! The current PR adds extended audio types explicitly (as the API requires type-checking to construct correct file parts), but you're right that a wildcard `audio/*` approach would be more maintainable.

The reason image and video use wildcards is because they're passed through as data URIs with their MIME type preserved — the provider doesn't need to know the specific subtype. Audio is handled differently here because we need to map MIME types to format strings for the `input_audio` content type.

That said, wildcard matching for audio (i.e. `mimeType.startsWith('audio/')`) would be the cleanest approach and matches how image/video wildcards work. I can update the PR to use `audio/*` wildcard matching instead of the explicit list if the maintainers prefer that approach — would just need to remove the `getAudioFormat` helper and pass the MIME type through directly.

