@aayush-kapoor Fair point — the original issue reporter [explicitly noted the Anthropic API error](https://github.com/vercel/ai/issues/13013) that occurs when `server_tool_use` and `tool_use` blocks are out of order.

Here is a minimal self-contained reproduction using the public conversion function directly (no API key needed):

```ts
import { convertToAnthropicMessagesPrompt } from "@ai-sdk/anthropic/internal";

const result = await convertToAnthropicMessagesPrompt({
  prompt: [
    { role: "user", content: [{ type: "text", text: "Search the web and also call my custom tool" }] },
    {
      role: "assistant",
      content: [
        // custom tool call comes FIRST (as the model might return them)
        { type: "tool-call", toolCallId: "tc1", toolName: "myTool", args: {} },
        // web_search tool result (provider-executed) comes AFTER
        { type: "tool-result", toolCallId: "ws1", toolName: "web_search", content: [{ type: "text", text: "results" }], isError: false },
      ],
    },
  ],
  modelId: "claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022",
  sendReasoning: false,
});

// Without the fix, the assistant message content would be:
// [ tool_use(myTool), web_search_tool_result ]
// — Anthropic API rejects this with 400: server_tool_use must precede tool_use.
//
// With the fix, it becomes:
// [ web_search_tool_result, tool_use(myTool) ]
// — which is accepted.

console.log(JSON.stringify(result.prompt.messages[1].content, null, 2));
```

The Anthropic API error this prevents:
```
BadRequestError: 400 { "type": "error", "error": { "type": "invalid_request_error",
  "message": "content: server_tool_use and web_search_tool_result blocks must appear before tool_use blocks" } }
```

This is a real ordering constraint enforced server-side. The fix is a targeted sort that only activates when both `server_tool_use`/`web_search_tool_result` and regular `tool_use`/`tool_result` coexist in the same turn, so it is a no-op for all standard single-tool-type conversations.

