Hi @aayush-kapoor, thanks for the review!

The upstream issue is [opencode#28427](https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode/issues/28427) — users hit this when connecting to OpenAI-compatible servers that return `"role": ""` in streaming delta chunks.

**Minimal reproduction:**

```ts
import { createOpenAICompatible } from "@ai-sdk/openai-compatible";
import { streamText } from "ai";

const provider = createOpenAICompatible({
  name: "test",
  baseURL: "https://open.bigmodel.cn/api/paas/v4", // zhipu GLM-5, or any server returning empty-string role
});

const { textStream } = streamText({
  model: provider.chatModel("glm-4-flash"),
  prompt: "Say hello",
});

for await (const chunk of textStream) {
  console.log(chunk);
}
// Throws: AI_TypeValidationError — role validation fails on `"role": ""`
```

The error occurs because `chunkBaseSchema` uses `z.enum(["assistant"]).nullish()` which rejects `""`. An empty string is neither `"assistant"` nor `null`/`undefined`, so Zod throws.

The `role` field on delta chunks is not consumed by the SDK — it only exists for schema validation — so relaxing to `z.string().nullish()` is safe and matches the provider-agnostic intent of the openai-compatible adapter.

The HMAC note is worth following up on. HMAC requires the verifier to hold the same secret, so "third-party verification" becomes key distribution. Ed25519 doesn't have that problem. Public key at a URL; anyone verifies without touching your signing material.

[AgentLair](https://agentlair.dev) already ships this for Vercel AI SDK agents. Agent Auth Tokens are EdDSA (Ed25519) JWTs per session, public key at `https://agentlair.dev/.well-known/jwks.json`. The callback integration maps to:

```typescript
const result = await generateText({
